- Efficient functional implementation:
  - hash tables don't work well: adding <mouse,4> to a bucket would overwrite/destroy the shared chain (m1 = {bat↦1, camel↦2, dog↦3}; if index(camel)=index(mouse)=5, then Hash(mouse) -> <mouse,4> and m1 is gone). Copying the (large) array for every extension is not efficient. (slides 14–15)
  - → use balanced binary search trees: adding a binding creates d new nodes along the root-to-insertion-point path (rebuild only the path), share all other subtrees; m1 unchanged; lookup O(log n) for a balanced tree. (slides 16–17)
